============================GS SendRequest Request Codes============================Modification History:30-Mar-95 Dave Lyons	Allocated 7F00..7FFF for A2PRO (Tim Tobin / Lunatic Bruce			E'Sex, a2pro@genie.geis.com). 3-Sep-92 Dave Lyons	Created file from 6.0 Interface files + 6.0.1 stuff 8-Sep-92 Dave Lyons	Added systemSaysDoClipboard.21-Oct-92 Dave Lyons	Added srqQuit and srqOpenOrPrint.==================================================================================Here is the list of globally-defined SendRequest request codes, which are inthe range $0000..7FFF.Do no assign a global code from $8000..FFFF; these are reserved for definitionwithin various name domains (anybody who invents a unique prefix string gets todefine the non-global codes any way the want to).SUGGESTED CONVENTIONSFor requests that are mainly sent by a particular tool set, put the tool setnumber as the high byte of the request code.  If a particular toolbox call willbe sending the code, you can even put the function number in the other byte.This gives things like $0502 being sent by DeskStartUp (toolbox function $0205).So they don't match, but there's some order to it.The $00xx codes are for random miscellaneous things.  If the Tool Locator sendsany codes, they probably go here, since the $01xx codes are already taken for theFinder.If there is some reason to start in on a completely new range of codes, we canwork down from $7FFF quite a ways before we collide with system tool set numbers(the highest tool set these days is Media Controller, $26).A few of the codes are mnemonic in stupid ways, like $000E for Ejecting and$000D for Force Undim.  I'll try not to get too cute.==================================================================================0001 = systemSaysBeep, sent by SysBeep20002 = systemSaysUnknownDisk, sent by HandleDiskInsert0003 = srqGoAway0004 = srqGetrSoundSample0005 = srqSynchronize0006 = srqPlayrSoundSample0008 = systemSaysNewDeskMsg, sent by Desktop in Window Manager000C = systemSaysDoClipboard (sent by Scrap Manager in 6.0.1)000D = systemSaysForceUndim (in 6.0.1, GS/OS sends before alerts; SysBeep2 sends)000E = systemSaysEjectingDev (sent by HandleDiskInsert & used by EasyMount 1.0)0010 = srqOpenOrPrint (check MessageCenter for msg $0011)0011 = srqQuit01xx = reserved for Finder0100 = finderSaysHello0101 = finderSaysGoodbye0102 = finderSaysSelectionChanged0103 = finderSaysMItemSelected0104 = finderSaysBeforeOpen0105 = finderSaysOpenFailed0106 = finderSaysBeforeCopy0107 = finderSaysIdle0108 = finderSaysExtrasChosen0109 = finderSaysBeforeRename010A = finderSaysKeyHit0502 = systemSaysDeskStartUp0503 = systemSaysDeskShutDown051E = systemSaysFixedAppleMenu0F01 = systemSaysMenuKey1201 = systemSaysGetSysIcon (new for 6.0.1; sent by GetSysIcon in QDAux)7F00..7FFF = *** Allocated by A2PRO *** (see above)8000+ = defined within unique request-procedure name domains[end of document]